body:
@annevk, as you mentioned, we need to sort this out clearly. Currently both Blink and Gecko return null for about:blank. This is contrary to https://slightlyoff.github.io/ServiceWorker/spec/service_worker/index.html#selection that says a client with a local url should inherit its parent frame's registration. I think I'm leaning towards making the local url clients' active worker return null. Is there any point we should make them inherit their parent's active worker? Do they actually need to be controlled?

For srcdoc iframes with allow-same-origin case, I agree it should inherit its parent's active worker.

/cc @jakearchibald
